2.25.1

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
free_transition_pgtable();
init_transition_pgtable();
machine_kexec_cleanup();
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because both `init_transition_pgtable()` and `machine_kexec_cleanup()` (for 64-bit) or `machine_kexec_alloc_page_tables()` and `machine_kexec_cleanup()` (for 32-bit) attempt to free the same memory pages when memory allocation fails during the kexec load process, resulting in a double free scenario.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
image->arch.pgd = NULL;
image->arch.pmd0 = NULL;
image->arch.pte0 = NULL;
```
Reason:
The patch fixes the bug by setting the pointers to NULL after freeing the memory pages, ensuring that subsequent calls to free the same pages do not occur, thus preventing the double free issue.

